WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.856
Lukas: We've covered the technical exercise now. What questions do you have about our team?

2
00:00:05.856 --> 00:00:14.664
Raj: How does engineering onboarding cover unsafe operations? Just to confirm, new engineers get sandbox access, right?

3
00:00:14.664 --> 00:00:23.089
Hannah: Yes, with a mentor and scoped permissions. Production changes need review and explicit approval.

4
00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:29.689
Raj: Mentors walk you through approvals, right? Sorry, I mean the production review process.

5
00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:37.273
Raj: How much bandwidth do mentors usually reserve? Maybe pairing early prevents repeated safety mistakes.

6
00:00:37.273 --> 00:00:44.881
Lukas: We reserve pairing time during initial weeks. Small changes get feedback before larger independent work.

7
00:00:44.881 --> 00:00:50.761
Raj: How do you close the loop on incidents? Does each action item get an owner?

8
00:00:50.761 --> 00:00:59.714
Hannah: Yes, owners provide evidence at follow-up reviews. We track completion, not just ticket creation.

9
00:00:59.714 --> 00:01:07.562
Raj: That helps me understand your engineering expectations. I'd also ask how testing time gets protected.

10
00:01:07.562 --> 00:01:15.890
Raj: Thanks, those answers address my main concerns. I'd enjoy learning within those clear safety boundaries.

